message: "If you use these results, programs or data, please cite this repository."
title: "Erdős Problem #817: the exact value g_3(7) = 474 and related computations"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "rb06716"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-23"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rb06716/erdos-817"
keywords:
  - Erdős problems
  - Erdős–Sárközy function
  - subset sums
  - arithmetic progressions
  - additive combinatorics
  - exhaustive search
  - OEIS A399720
abstract: >-
  Computations for the Erdős–Sárközy function g_k(n) (Erdős Problem #817, OEIS A399720): the least N such that
  some n-element subset of {1,...,N} has subset sums with no non-constant k-term arithmetic progression.
  Main result: g_3(7) = 474, attained only by {302, 409, 447, 459, 465, 466, 474}. The proof is
  computer-assisted: a certificate for the upper bound, and an exhaustive search for the lower bound, run by two
  independently written programs that agree on the full per-level counts for every N <= 478. Also included:
  certified upper bounds for g_3(8..14), the values g_4(1..7) and g_5(1..8), a correction to a claim about n = 6
  made in 2002 and 2003, and verification tools. The package was produced with the assistance of an AI agent
  (Claude, Anthropic).
